{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal #11</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">2025 CEMC Cayley #8</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lies on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19ade8bdcd8616ec49efff1d770a268c5bf21d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AD = CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b32b0e3a7b30dfc755979e3554668eb37ec48784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = 80^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b591cd4cbc3cd3d8746972dae656279220ce9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACD$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e33f77e1f4086c17415cf551e287c6440b988d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 20^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 60^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 80^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 100^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 40^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"481\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b3845d5da2053055d8f4e4fb8fea8c08fb359fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AD$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2cd51fcfe7516d94760633751f58f1df6499fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ABD = m \\angle ADB = 80^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"222\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718105456aa41c974333e9ffe73a31053003c68b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c28b8d709d3b873ec6db017839b1520919db39db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> form a straight angle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e06044256ca40ef3b7688052a8838b9532f57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ADC = 180^{\\circ} - m \\angle ADB = 180^{\\circ} - 80^{\\circ} = 100^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"395\" height=\"16\" />. We can now only focus on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Because the sum of the interior angles in any triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b5a79c3d5a743e40809159498f5b67271c94cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be a number, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b763d411d6683a5dd725b3b1f7018d46a7b5c5f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ACD = m \\angle DAC = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"205\" height=\"14\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc4cbeb7e82c3193cd6e81ded08612b8aa907e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100^{\\circ} + x + x = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d64b432c4e78b86b24dcd5e0687bfc15059e9c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 100^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0dea81ddb3a2bb05fd53c5237e88c22af6e34d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 180^{\\circ} - 100^{\\circ} = 80^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cff9b6c1f9218c92e5be9be3464e6518e8720bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{80^{\\circ}}{2} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 40^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 